# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Curio — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env* is gitignored (only .env.example is
# tracked). Never commit real values. Do NOT set non-essential cookies via any
# of these before consent (RGPD, brief rule 3).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase ──
# NON-NEGOTIABLE (RGPD): the Supabase project MUST be provisioned in the EU
# Frankfurt region (eu-central-1). Both values come from the Supabase project:
# Settings → API. The URL is public (NEXT_PUBLIC_), the anon key is public too.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Service-role key — SERVER ONLY, never NEXT_PUBLIC. Bypasses RLS; used for the
# few trusted server writes/reads (invitation tokens, and the RGPD consent_logs
# journal, which must record anonymous visitors whose user_id is null — an insert
# RLS denies to anon/authenticated clients). Lives only in .env.local.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# ── Site ──
# Canonical origin for SEO metadata (canonical URLs, hreflang, OG, sitemap).
# On Vercel set this to the production domain. Defaults to localhost in dev.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── PostHog Cloud EU (analytics) ──
# EU cloud only (host pinned to eu.i.posthog.com in lib/analytics/config.ts —
# data must not leave the EU). OPT-IN STRICT: the SDK is not even loaded before
# the user grants analytics consent (lib/analytics/index.ts). Leave unset to
# keep analytics fully inert.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=your-posthog-project-key

# ── Axeptio (CMP cookies) ──
# Consent is handled today by a first-party banner (decision D006): on-brand,
# EN/FR, strict opt-in, writing the consent_logs journal. Axeptio's hosted
# widget is a pluggable provider behind the same store — set this client id to
# swap it in. No cookie is set by default before consent.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AXEPTIO_CLIENT_ID=your-axeptio-client-id
